# Every text file checks out with LF on every platform, whatever the
# checkout's core.autocrlf, so a contributor or CI runner on Windows reads
# the same bytes the release builds from. Go gates byte-compare checked-out
# files (TestBaselineFileIsFrozen pins the sha256 of
# internal/store/migrations/00001_baseline.sql; the drift canary
# byte-compares internal/store/schema_snapshot.sql against a regeneration),
# and a CRLF rewrite nobody authored would trip them. text=auto leaves
# binary files untouched.
#
# [LAW:one-source-of-truth] The bytes on disk must equal the bytes the embed
# package sees, on every platform, every checkout. A platform-dependent
# normalization is a second source the gates cannot distinguish from a real
# edit. [LAW:single-enforcer] This file is the one place line endings are
# decided; no workflow or script sets core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf
